@nsobid-FA3897E0FADDD49C69ED00F23E705B3E

# Splatoon 2 1.1.0 QA Build 2 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables every post-process anti-aliasing pass.
//
// All of the game's AA is agl::pfx::FilterAA, drawn at the end of
// gsys::ModelSceneBuffer::drawFinalImage. Its modes are FXAA, ReduceAA and a
// draw callback. The game's GfxMgr binds its own SMAA (edge detection, blend
// weights, neighborhood blending) to that callback when it loads a scene, so
// SMAA, not FXAA, is the AA normally drawn.
//
// Whether the filter runs is one test: the scene allows AA, the filter is
// enabled, and its scale is above zero. It is inlined into each function that
// plans or draws the frame: calcView picks the scene's render target,
// allocRenderBuffer sizes it, and drawFinalImage routes the image through the
// filter (isFilterAAEnabled is the out-of-line copy). Each copy now takes its
// false result, so the scene renders straight to the final target as it does
// when a scene turns the filter off, and no AA pass runs whatever mode or
// parameters a scene or environment file selects.

@enabled
013B3A30 05000014   // B to the AA-off result in calcView (was LDR S0,[X,#0xA58] = FilterAA scale)
013B3C18 06000014   // B to the AA-off result in isFilterAAEnabled (was LDR S0,[X,#0xA58] = FilterAA scale)
013B614C 09000014   // B to the AA-off result in allocRenderBuffer (was LDR S0,[X,#0xA58] = FilterAA scale)
013B67F8 04000014   // B to the AA-off result in drawFinalImage (was LDR S0,[X,#0xA58] = FilterAA scale)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against this symbol-bearing build (agl/gsys + Lp +
// sead, NVN); every site was located by symbol and byte-verified against the
// IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
